fn to_english_time(seconds: u64) -> String {
    if seconds == 0 {
        return "0 seconds".to_string();
    }

    let hours = seconds / 3600;
    let minutes = (seconds % 3600) / 60;
    let remaining_seconds = seconds % 60;

    let mut result = String::new();

    if hours > 0 {
        result.push_str(&format!("{} hour", hours));
        if hours > 1 {
            result.push('s');
        }
    }

    if minutes > 0 {
        if !result.is_empty() {
            result.push_str(" ");
        }
        result.push_str(&format!("{} minute", minutes));
        if minutes > 1 {
            result.push('s');
        }
    }

    if remaining_seconds > 0 {
        if !result.is_empty() {
            result.push_str(" ");
        }
        result.push_str(&format!("{} second", remaining_seconds));
        if remaining_seconds > 1 {
            result.push('s');
        }
    }

    result
}
```

This solution first calculates the number of hours, minutes, and remaining seconds from the input time in seconds. Then, it constructs the English representation of the time by appending the appropriate units and values to a string based on the calculated hours, minutes, and seconds. Finally, it returns the constructed string as the result."}]

